      "id": 221098,
      "name": "Matchstickman",
      "username": "Matchstickman",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/matchstickman/{size}/1880_2.png",
      "created_at": "2018-08-08T11:22:26.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Foote\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/48/1877_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Foote:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>On Medico, I’m curious about how the interactions work between his base Clinical Consult power and the card Second Opinion. Let’s say one other target has the Consult buff while Second Opinion is in play and Medico heals that target for 1 HP. Consult increases this to 3 HP which triggers Second Opinions option. Let’s now say that the other hero chooses to use the power and not regain the health. Does that target continue to have the Consult buff since no HP was regained? Does the Consult buff get swallowed to trigger Second Opinion? Would Second Opinion trigger at all due to me misplaying Consult be a possibility?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Second Opinion would trigger. (W)Rest your mind on the possibility of you getting that wrong first.</p>\n<p>While testing I played it as if the buff went away, much like how DW Setback's base power damage reduction would go away if Mr Fixer was hit for 4 damage but redirected it away with Driving Mantis because the damage was reduced to 2 (by DW Setback)- it had been used, even if not for it's original purpose (and the video game backs this up).</p>",
