      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/{size}/1877_2.png",
      "created_at": "2018-08-08T14:01:02.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Matchstickman\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/matchstickman/48/1880_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Matchstickman:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>If only there was some way you could have had some input into the creation of this card!&nbsp; <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/stuck_out_tongue.png?v=12\" title=\":stuck_out_tongue:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":stuck_out_tongue:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Hahaha so true! Most of my contributions were early-mid development and even then Comandora wasn’t a deck I played much.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>It’s just so odd to me that there is a LOT of text on that card that seems so meaningless and inconsequential. We always battle in play testing about text length and what will/won’t fit. There has got to be a particular and specific use for that wall of text or it wouldn’t be there, and honestly I just want to know what it is I’m missing. The other possibility listed in this thread cannot be the purpose for that text wall. It would have never made it out of PT. When I have time later I’ll go back through the PT forum if it’s still accessible.&nbsp;</p>",
